  "question": {
    "text": "Consider the dissociation of the weak acid \\(\\mathrm{HX}\\) as given below\n\\(\\mathrm{HX}(\\mathrm{aq}) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}^{+}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{X}^{-}(\\mathrm{aq}), \\mathrm{Ka}=1.2 \\times 10^{-5}\\)\n\\(\\left[\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}\\right.\\) : dissociation constant \\(]\\)\nThe osmotic pressure of \\(0.03 \\mathrm{M}\\) aqueous solution of \\(\\mathrm{HX}\\) at \\(300 \\mathrm{~K}\\) is _______ \\(\\times 10^{-2}\\) bar (nearest integer).\n[Given : \\(\\mathrm{R}=0.083 \\mathrm{~L} \\mathrm{bar} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1} \\mathrm{~K}^{-1}\\)]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "76",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{HX} \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}^{+}+\\mathrm{X}^{-} \\quad \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}=1.2 \\times 10^{-5} \\\\\n& 0.03 \\mathrm{M} \\\\\n& 0.03-\\mathrm{x} \\quad \\mathrm{x} \\quad \\mathrm{x} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{a}}=1.2 \\times 10^{-5}=\\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{0.03-\\mathrm{x}} \\\\\n& 0.03-\\mathrm{x} \\approx 0.03\\left(\\mathrm{~K}_{\\mathrm{a}} \\text { is very small }\\right) \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{x}^2}{0.03}=1.2 \\times 10^{-5} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{x}=6 \\times 10^{-4}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Final solution : $0.03-x+x+x$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& =0.03+x=0.03+6 \\times 10^{-4} \\\\\n& \\Pi=\\left(0.03+\\left(6 \\times 10^{-4}\\right)\\right) \\times 0.083 \\times 300 \\\\\n& =76.19 \\times 10^{-2} \\approx 76 \\times 10^{-2}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
